emical Engineering","years":[2008,2009]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I99065089","name":"Tsinghua University","years":[2008]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I27357992","name":"Dalian University of Technology","years":[2007]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4391767660","name":"State Key Laboratory of Fine Chemicals","years":[2007]}],"author_id":"A5100342351","ca_plastic_works_count":2,"ca_works_count":2,"citations_by_year":[{"all":206,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":211,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":260,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":281,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":334,"plastic":0,"year":2021},{"all":363,"plastic":0,"year":2022},{"all":362,"plastic":0,"year":2023},{"all":368,"plastic":1,"year":2024},{"all":408,"plastic":14,"year":2025},{"all":334,"plastic":25,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":4349,"current_in_ca":true,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":2007,"first_year":2026,"h_index":28,"institution_ids":["I36053171"],"last_ca_year":2026,"last_year":2026,"m_quotient":1.47,"name":"Kun Zhang","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0970-3234","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":40,"plastic_works_count":2,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I36053171","name":"California State University, Chico","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I19820366","name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210110024","name":"Institute of Applied Ecology","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210165038","name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":58,"rising_score":0.0028,"work_count":2,"work_ids":["W4391998425","W7225641200"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"Plastic mulches have become an essential component of modern agriculture since their introduction in the 1950s. However, disposal of plastic mulches poses serious environmental challenges as plastics that are not considered biodegradable or compostable can take several hundred years to degrade. Each year in the United States, only 9% of overall plastic waste is recycled while 79% is accumulated in landfills or the natural environment. Recycling of plastic mulch is especially constrained due to their contamination that results from their use in farming. Currently, recovered mulches are reported to have 30\u201380% surface contamination, primarily from soil and plant debris. Plastic mulch waste is concentrated in areas where they are used and can provide logistical opportunities to the plastic recycling industries. Plastic recycling includes mechanical, advanced (chemical and thermal), and biological methods, that may all be used for polyethylene (PE). Most plastic is recycled using the mechanical method, while advanced and biological methods are promising but face significant financial and technical challenges. For all recycling methods, strategies are needed for managing surface contamination to realize the recycling potential of plastic mulch.","author_count":7,"author_ids":["A5005241379","A5024182790","A5031841217","A5093970331","A5100342351","A5104246838","A5108316934"],"author_institution_ids":["I36053171"],"authors":[{"id":"A5024182790","name":"Kwabena Agyarko Sarpong"},{"id":"A5104246838","name":"Funmilayo A. Adesina"},{"id":"A5031841217","name":"Lisa Wasko DeVetter"},{"id":"A5100342351","name":"Kun Zhang"},{"id":"A5093970331","name":"Kevin DeWhitt"},{"id":"A5005241379","name":"Karl R. Englund"},{"id":"A5108316934","name":"Carol A. Miles"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":40,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.48130/cas-0024-0003","domain_tags":["soil_and_agriculture"],"facet_tags":["matrix:soil_and_agriculture"],"institution_ids":["I36053171","I4210096079","I4210125207","I72951846"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Circular Agricultural Systems","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"diamond","oa_url":"https://www.maxapress.com/data/article/cas/preview/pdf/cas-0024-0003.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10389","T10753","T14179"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-01-01","study_type":"article","title":"Recycling agricultural plastic mulch: limitations and opportunities in the United States","type":"article","work_id":"W4391998425","year":2024},{"abstract":"Abstract Polyethylene plastic mulch (PE mulch) has been increasingly used by specialty crop growers to improve crop yield and quality. However, most PE mulch after use ends up in landfills, causing plastic pollution. The challenge of recycling agricultural PE mulch waste is due to its high contaminant content. To address this challenge and promote the recycling of PE mulch, this study explored the processing of PE mulch waste and used it as a modifier in asphalt paving materials. The results of performance tests showed that the addition of PE mulch stiffened asphalt binders, which benefited rutting resistance, but slightly compromised cracking resistance. Recycled PE mulch had a lower effectiveness to modify asphalt binders than virgin PE mulch because of its lower effective plastic content. The dry mixing method is recommended to incorporate PE mulch waste into mixtures, as it has a lower adverse effect on cracking resistance than the wet mixing method.","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5005241379","A5034304672","A5100342351","A5100423973","A5104246838","A5161321878"],"author_institution_ids":["I36053171"],"authors":[{"id":"A5100342351","name":"Kun Zhang"},{"id":"A5104246838","name":"Funmilayo A. Adesina"},{"id":"A5161321878","name":"Yuefeng Zhu"},{"id":"A5100423973","name":"Hui Li"},{"id":"A5005241379","name":"Karl R. Englund"},{"id":"A5034304672","name":"Jinru Chen"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1061/jpeodx.pveng-2286","domain_tags":["soil_and_agriculture"],"facet_tags":["matrix:soil_and_agriculture"],"institution_ids":["I137902535","I36053171","I72951846"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Transportation Engineering Part B Pavements","last_updated":"2026-11-11T12:16:26.678958","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1061/jpeodx.pveng-2286","openalex_topics":["T10264","T10389","T13140"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10264","pub_date":"2026-11-09","study_type":"article","title":"Recycling Agricultural Plastic Mulch Waste into a Modifier in Asphalt Paving Materials","type":"article","work_id":"W7225641200","year":2026}]}
